{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q105439","formula":"CaSO₄","hill":"CaO4S","elements":["O","S","Ca"],"composition":{"O":4.0,"S":1.0,"Ca":1.0},"names":{"en":"Anhydrite","ru":"Ангидрит","uk":"Ангідрит"},"descriptions":{"en":"Anhydrite, or anhydrous calcium sulfate, is a mineral with the chemical formula CaSO4. It is in the orthorhombic crystal system, with three directions of perfect cleavage parallel to the three planes of symmetry. It is not isomorphous with the orthorhombic barium (baryte) and strontium (celestine) sulfates, as might be expected from the chemical formulas.","ru":"Ангидри́т (др.-греч. ἀν- — приставка отрицания и ὕδωρ — «вода», то есть «лишённый воды») — минерал класса сульфатов, безводный сульфат кальция. При добавлении воды увеличивается в объёме примерно на 60 % и постепенно превращается в гипс.","uk":"Ангідри́т (рос. ангидрит: англ. anhydrite; нім."},"fame":50,"pubchemCid":null,"mass":null,"charge":0,"smiles":null,"inchikey":null,"iupac":null,"classes":[{"qid":"Q12089225","names":{"en":"mineral species","ru":"действительный вид минералов","uk":"мінеральний вид"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"crystal","source":"materialsproject","ref":"mp-3082","atoms":24,"license":"CC BY 4.0, Materials Project"},"structure":{"cell":[[6.974,0.0,0.0],[-3.487,6.04,0.0],[0.0,0.0,6.275]],"kind":"crystal","atoms":[{"x":-1.744,"y":3.02,"z":4.183,"el":"Ca"},{"x":5.231,"y":3.02,"z":4.183,"el":"Ca"},{"x":1.744,"y":3.02,"z":2.092,"el":"Ca"},{"x":3.487,"y":0.0,"z":0.0,"el":"Ca"},{"x":3.487,"y":0.0,"z":6.275,"el":"Ca"},{"x":0.0,"y":6.04,"z":0.0,"el":"Ca"},{"x":0.0,"y":6.04,"z":6.275,"el":"Ca"},{"x":-1.744,"y":3.02,"z":1.046,"el":"S"},{"x":5.231,"y":3.02,"z":1.046,"el":"S"},{"x":1.744,"y":3.02,"z":5.229,"el":"S"},{"x":3.487,"y":0.0,"z":3.138,"el":"S"},{"x":0.0,"y":6.04,"z":3.138,"el":"S"},{"x":2.034,"y":1.879,"z":6.115,"el":"O"},{"x":4.33,"y":0.822,"z":4.024,"el":"O"},{"x":4.097,"y":3.339,"z":1.932,"el":"O"},{"x":-0.61,"y":2.701,"z":1.932,"el":"O"},{"x":0.843,"y":5.217,"z":2.252